@lolannn/dsh-effort-slider README · Why a model switch remaps the effort：The Host validates the triple, it does not normalize it. In
`@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` → `resolveCallWithInfo`:

```js
const reasoning = info.reasoning;
const requested = defaulted.reasoningEffort;
if (reasoning === void 0) {
  if (requested !== void 0) throw new LlmError(`... does not support reasoning effort "${requested}"`, "UNSUPPORTED_REASONING_EFFORT");

@lolannn/dsh-effort-slider README · Why a model switch remaps the effort：The last real choice is remembered in `lastEffort`, so
`max → 无档位模型 → back` returns to `max` instead of that model's default: the
intent survives the models that cannot express it.

@lolannn/dsh-effort-slider README · Why every visible label is passed through `safeLabel`：Every label rendered as text therefore runs through `safeLabel()`, which turns
`/` and `\` into ` · `. `aria-label` and `title` keep the raw identifier, because
they are attributes and the guard only reads `textContent`.
